        <mxCell id="WWpYAckt_C0c_vEcJ-f6-2" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;step 3.4&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Create a Queue Pair. The Queue paor os the fundamental object that lets you talk directly to the NIC hardware bypassin the kernel&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;This create two queue:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SQ (Send Queue)&lt;/b&gt; - Post work requests here and NIC reads and executes them&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RQ (Receive Queue)&lt;/b&gt; - Post buffers here and NIC writes incomming data into them&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="625" y="670" width="445" height="220" as="geometry" />
